# Projects made before `add_project` resolved a bare name against the
# projects directory. A name typed into the window resolved against
# whatever directory the server was started from, which for a checkout
# is this repository - so they are here, they are somebody else's git,
# and `git add -A` has committed two of them as gitlinks.
# Nothing is moved or deleted here: they are somebody's work, and all
# this does is stop them being noise in `git status`.
